  kicker="The condition"
  description="Vitiligo destroys melanocytes outright, which is why a pigment drug alone can't fix it. The melanocortin angle is a combination: narrowband UVB helps bring pigment cells back into the white patches, and the MC1R agonist afamelanotide then drives them to repigment — a two-step that works better than either alone."
  thread="A switch is no use without a bulb — so first the skin must be given back its pigment cells, and only then told to shine."
  updated="2026"
